COMMAND NAME: mpprebuildseg.sh

Rebuilds segment instances from the MPP system catalog tables of 
a Bizgres MPP master instance.

*****************************************************
SYNOPSIS
*****************************************************

mpprebuildseg.sh -d <master_data_directory> [-a] [-q] 
[-l <logfile_directory>]

mpprebuildseg.sh [-? | -v]


*****************************************************
DESCRIPTION
*****************************************************

The mpprebuildseg.sh script builds segment instances using configuration 
information contained in the MPP system catalog tables of a Bizgres MPP 
master instance. The use of this script assumes that you have:

* Built a master instance from a backup file using mpprebuildcluster.sh -m.

* Have edited the MPP system catalog tables on the MPP master instance to 
  reflect your desired system configuration. See the Bizgres MPP 
  Administrator Guide for the MPP schema reference. 


*****************************************************
OPTIONS
*****************************************************

-d <master_data_directory>

Required. The data directory of the MPP master instance.

-a

Do not prompt the user for confirmation.

-q

Run in quiet mode. Command output is not displayed on the screen, 
but is still written to the log file.

-l <logfile_directory>

The directory to write the log file. Defaults to ~/mppAdminLogs.

-?

Displays the online help.

-v

Displays the version, status, last updated date, and check sum of this script.


*****************************************************
EXAMPLES
*****************************************************

Rebuild the segment instances using the data found in the given MPP master:

mpprebuildseg.sh -d /mpp_master_data


